Enable `in` parameter semantics by default

`in` parameters now use the behavior previously selected by `-preview=in`:
they are `const scope`, accept rvalues, and non-pointer parameters are passed by
reference. Pointer parameters are passed by value because they are already
references.

The `-preview=in` switch remains accepted for compatibility. Projects that need
the previous behavior can use the new `-revert=in` switch.

For more information, see the specification for
$(LINK2 https://dlang.org/spec/function.html#in-params, `in` parameters).
